# BAND — TBD AT LAUNCH. THIS AGENT CLAIMED NOTHING.

`launch_local.sh` refuses to launch the cell until a sibling file named
**`BAND_CLAIMED`** (no extension) exists next to this one. That file is the
orchestrator's to drop, and only after it has decided the question below.

## The question is unusual for this round, and worth reading before answering

⭐ **E-1b draws NO new decks.** Every world is a permutation of the *unseen tail*
of an already-archived E4 game, generated by

```
world_rng(deck_seed, ply, world)
   = Random(WORLD_SEED ^ deck_seed*1000003 ^ ply*7919 ^ world*104729)
```

where `deck_seed` is **the archive's own** seed. No seed in any registered deck
band is consumed, no new band is spent, and none retires as
`decision_influenced`. E-1b also produces **no `results.csv` elo row** — it is a
per-ply price in realized points, not a head-to-head.

E-1a (`measurement/e4_continuation_20260828`) claimed no band either, for
exactly this reason.

So the launch gate here is **not** "claim a band"; it is **"acknowledge that no
band is being spent, deliberately"** — the same fail-closed posture S1's
`run_g3.sh` takes, for the opposite reason. A round that silently spends a band
and a round that silently spends none are both failures of the same discipline.

## What the orchestrator should do

1. Confirm the above by reading `continue_armed.py::world_rng` and
   `PREREG.md` §11 — do not take this file's word for it.
2. Decide whether any registry entry is owed. The house position on E-1a was
   **no**; if the orchestrator agrees, no `governance/BAND_REGISTRY.csv` append
   is required.
3. Drop the acknowledgement file, e.g.

   ```bash
   D=measurement/e1b_armed_continuation_20260901
   cat > $D/BAND_CLAIMED <<'EOF'
   NO BAND SPENT. E-1b re-prices frozen banked plies and draws no new decks;
   every world is a permutation of an archived game's unseen tail under the
   archive's own deck_seed. No BAND_REGISTRY.csv append is owed. No
   results.csv elo row will be written. Acknowledged by the orchestrator
   <date>, after reading continue_armed.py::world_rng and PREREG §11.
   EOF
   ```

4. Then stamp `BLIND_COMMIT.json` (the freeze commit's 40-hex sha) — the
   launcher checks that too — and launch.

⛔ This agent did not create `BAND_CLAIMED`, did not touch
`governance/BAND_REGISTRY.csv`, and did not launch the cell.
